From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: crypto: sun8i-ce - Add RSA, ECDH and ECDSA verification for the H616

The H616 crypto engine has a public key unit (algorithms RSA 0x20 and
ECC 0x21) for RSA 512-4096 and ECC up to 521 bits. Register for the
H616:
- rsa: modular exponentiation for 512, 1024, 2048, 3072 and 4096-bit
  moduli, rsa-generic as fallback for other sizes;
- ecdh-nist-p192/p256/p384: point multiplication;
- ecdsa-nist-p192/p256/p384/p521: the engine's signature verification.

A task gives the operands in order in the source, each one operand
width long and little endian (as the vendor U-Boot sunxi_rsa_calc()
does); the width in words and the operation go in the asymmetric
control word (user manual 10.1.3.4 and 10.1.3.10). Key checks, key
generation and the public key check stay in software, as in the generic
implementations. The tasks run one at a time on channel 3, which the
TRNG already uses; RSA and ECDH go through that channel's crypto engine,
ECDSA verification (a synchronous API) runs directly.

All register below the software implementations, like the engine's
other new modes: the CPU stays the default and the engine is used when
it is asked for by driver name.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
